    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d40">

                <pb facs="0107" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1945v02/pg97"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Lot 55D 668, Box 2380</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of War</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Patterson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-11">December 11,
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For your information I am sending you a copy of a memorandum from General Groves
                    on certain questions in which I know your mission to Moscow is interested.</p>
                <p>I approve of paragraphs 1<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi>. No comment by me is necessary on paragraph 1<hi
                        rendition="#italic">c</hi> or paragraph 2 which merely reflect General
                    Groves’ views.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert</hi> P. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Patterson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d40-a1.xml" xpointer="d40-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
